hexagon: take the packed band path of the batch conv by default

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 plus the patches before this one in patches/series.

Files:
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/gdn-conv-ops.c  the default of GDN_CONV_F16_MODE

The problem

The patch that adds the packed band path leaves its default at 0, which is the f32 chain that
came before it. Thus the measured work does nothing until a build selects mode 4.

The change

The default becomes 4: f16 taps, a 16-bit qfloat accumulator, the int16 SiLU, and 3 token rows in
each iteration. Measured in tools/htp-lab, target gdn_chunk, 512 channels and 32 tokens on one
thread, against a float64 reference:

    mode 0, the f32 chain      115447 cycles   NMSE 2.7e-14
    mode 4, the packed band     31993 cycles   NMSE 3.0e-07

3.61 times faster. GDN_CONV_CHUNK is the largest single op of a 512-token prefill of the 4B, at
27 % of the time on the digital signal processor, thus this is the largest prefill change of
the series. The op runs when a batch has more than one token, thus it serves the prefill and
the speculative verify, and not the single-token decode step.

The error

3.0e-07 of NMSE against a baseline of 2.7e-14. The consumer of this output, the chunked gated
delta net, already measures 3.0e-07 of its own, and the bound that the backend tests apply is
2e-06, thus this value costs nothing downstream. It is a regression from an exact baseline and
a reviewer must see it. GDN_CONV_F16_MODE 0 takes the old path back.

Why this patch was out of the series between 2026-09-20 03:59 and this revision

The first form of the packed band path gave -Inf for a conv output in [14.4922, 15.7266]. The
model Qwen3.5-2B then gave one token again and again on the digital signal processor, and the
central processor and the graphics processor stayed correct. The cause was in the patch that
adds the path, not in this one, and the revision of that patch of 2026-09-20 holds the fix.
Refer to its text.

Two measurements decide whether mode 4 is safe, and neither of them is in this lab:

1. The conv output of the real model reaches the band. A forward pass of Qwen3.5-2B on the
   prompt "The capital of France is" gives 8 values in that band over 4 of the 18 gated delta
   net layers, and a 605-token prefill gives 699 over 13 layers.
2. The lab reaches the band only with an input range of 6 or more. The default of the target is
   4, thus every measurement before this revision stayed out of the band. The target of this
   revision has a phase that walks the f16 octaves, thus the default arguments now cover it.

Before this patch goes back into the series, do a test of the model on the phone and do a run of
the parity harness (llama-perplexity --kl-divergence against the central processor). The lab
proves the shape of the SiLU and the absence of a value that is not finite. It does not prove
the quality of the model, because an f16 accumulator over 4 taps cancels: at an input range of
4 the largest error of one value is 8.0e-03 at an output of 2.02.
diff -urN a/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/gdn-conv-ops.c b/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/gdn-conv-ops.c
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/gdn-conv-ops.c	2026-09-20 03:59:39.046281562 +0300
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/gdn-conv-ops.c	2026-09-20 03:59:39.062841780 +0300
@@ -192,7 +192,7 @@
 //   3  f16 taps, f16 accumulate, f16 SiLU. Every product goes back to f16 before the sum.
 //   4  the packed path: f16 taps, 32-bit accumulate, int16 SiLU, 4 token rows in each iteration.
 #ifndef GDN_CONV_F16_MODE
-#define GDN_CONV_F16_MODE 0
+#define GDN_CONV_F16_MODE 4
 #endif
 static int gdn_conv_f16_mode = GDN_CONV_F16_MODE;

